## Count data estimation

To answer this economic question we use count data model. Indeed, the dependent variable is the number of private lower secondary school within a city. This positive integer describe an intensity, justifying a count data model. 

Figures @fig-carte-colleges-prives and @fig-carte-colleges-publics map the number of private and public *collèges* per commune, computed from the Annuaire de l'Éducation and aggregated at the commune level.

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Number of collège per commune"}
::: {.column-screen}
::: {layout-ncol="2" layout-valign="top"}
![Number of private collèges per commune](carte_colleges_prives.png){#fig-carte-colleges-prives}

![Number of public collèges per commune](carte_colleges_publics.png){#fig-carte-colleges-publics}
:::
:::
::: 


```{r setup, include=FALSE, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE}
library(arrow); library(dplyr); library(ggplot2); library(kableExtra)

